# Nothing is enabled here: PAM setup is manual on Arch (see the PKGBUILD's
# header comment), so this only tells the user how.
post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
==> linux-hello-pam: PAM is NOT configured automatically on Arch.
    Enroll a face first (linux_hello_config, or `linux-hello enroll`), then
    add this line to /etc/pam.d/sudo, BEFORE its first `auth` line:

      auth  sufficient  pam_linux_hello.so context=sudo confirm

    Keep a root shell open while editing PAM files, and test with
    `sudo -k; sudo true` before closing it.
    polkit and the SDDM login screen: see "Manual setup on other
    distributions" in /usr/share/doc/linux-hello/PAM_MODULE.md
EOF
}
